<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Congress of Soviets of the Soviet Union</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1922">1922</a>–<a href="/years/1936">1936</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as All-Union Congress of Soviets</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Congress of Soviets of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> was the supreme organ of state power in the USSR from 1922 to 1936, made up of delegates from the soviets of the union republics. Its first session, on 30 December 1922, approved the treaty and declaration creating the Soviet Union. Between sessions power lay with its Central Executive Committee, and the 1936 constitution replaced it with the Supreme Soviet.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/congress-of-soviets-of-the-soviet-union.jpg" alt="Congress of Soviets of the Soviet Union" width="320" height="319" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TheSign 1998 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_the_Soviet_Union_(1923%E2%80%931936).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
